  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "An input string SSS of length NNN is transferred through the network using a special protocol. The protocol can send the string through a series of operations. In one operation, we can choose a lowercase english alphabet CCC and do **one** of the following:\n\n\nTransfer 111 copy of CCC through the network.\nTransfer 222 copies of CCC through the network.\nEach of the above transfers take 111 unit of time.\n\nFind the **minimum** time in which we can transfer the entire string SSS through the network.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line will contain TTT - the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nFirst line of each test case contains NNN - the length of the string SSS.\nSecond line of each test case contains the string SSS.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output in a single line, the minimum time required to transfer the string.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10510^5105.",
      "String SSS contains lowercase english alphabets only."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n5\ncbcdc\n6\naabeee",
        "output": "5\n4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 111: String can be transferred through following operations: send 111 copy of character c\\texttt{c}c, send 111 copy of character b\\texttt{b}b, send 111 copy of character c\\texttt{c}c, send 111 copy of character d\\texttt{d}d, and send 111 copy of character c\\texttt{c}c. Thus, total 555 operations are required.\nTest Case 222: String can be transferred through following operations: send 222 copies of character a\\texttt{a}a, send 111 copy of character b\\texttt{b}b, send 111 copy of character e\\texttt{e}e, and send 222 copies of character e\\texttt{e}e. Thus, total 444 operations are required."
      }
    ]
  },
